# Host-side input to nvs_partition_gen.py -- see README.md "Provisioning".
# Copy to provisioning.csv, fill in, generate the image, flash it once.
# Both the filled-in CSV and the generated .bin are gitignored.
#
# Two namespaces, read by two modules: "wifi" by wifi_station.c (stage 16),
# "mqtt" by the MQTT client (stage 17). One file and one flash provisions
# both -- the alternative, build-time Kconfig, would put the broker password
# in sdkconfig, which is gitignored and therefore not reproducible from a
# fresh clone.
key,type,encoding,value
wifi,namespace,,
ssid,data,string,YOUR_SSID_HERE
password,data,string,YOUR_PASSWORD_HERE
mqtt,namespace,,
# The broker host is the machine running docker compose, reached over the
# LAN -- not localhost, and not a container name. compose publishes 1883 on
# all interfaces from stage 17 (see ../compose.yaml).
host,data,string,192.168.1.100
# u16 rather than string so a typo fails in nvs_get_u16 naming the key,
# instead of silently becoming 0 in atoi.
port,data,u16,1883
# Must match RABBITMQ_USER / RABBITMQ_PASSWORD in the repo-root .env --
# the broker rejects anything else, and MQTT has no anonymous login here.
user,data,string,iot
password,data,string,YOUR_BROKER_PASSWORD_HERE
